From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:27:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max1720x: clear the alert bits with 0

Status's alert bits clear on writing 0; setting them leaves every
alert latched, so health reads dead from the first one on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/max1720x_battery.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max1720x_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max1720x_battery.c
index e2bd54ee3970..599adf763459 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max1720x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max1720x_battery.c
@@ -344,9 +344,12 @@ static int max172xx_battery_health(struct max1720x_device_info *info,
 	else
 		*health = POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_GOOD;
 
-	/* Clear events which are not self-clearing to detect next events */
+	/*
+	 * Clear events which are not self-clearing to detect next events;
+	 * writing 0 clears them
+	 */
 	if (status > 0 && status != MAX172XX_STATUS_IMX) {
-		ret = regmap_set_bits(info->regmap, MAX172XX_STATUS,
+		ret = regmap_clear_bits(info->regmap, MAX172XX_STATUS,
 				      MAX172XX_STATUS_VMN |
 				      MAX172XX_STATUS_VMX |
 				      MAX172XX_STATUS_TMN |
